It would be good to expand on this being very easily an anti-pattern: a `trait` with an `unsafe fn` associated item must be `unsafe` itself, unless the `unsafe fn` cannot be overriden (blanket `impl` for all possible implementors of the trait).

Otherwise the `unsafe fn` associated function becomes unusable within a non-`unsafe` generic function context, since each implementor is free to choose the narrow contract they want for that function.

  - Example

    ```rust
    trait DerefRead {
        unsafe fn deref_read (_: *const Self) -> Self
        ;
    }
    // Nothing prevents someone from doing
    impl DerefRead for ... {
        unsafe fn deref_read (_: *const Self) -> Read
        {
            ::core::ptr::null().read() // always UB
