If I could get a do-over at writing this method, I'd probably do it with less `mut`, less gratuitous shadowing, and more comments:
```suggestion
    fn fold<B, F>(mut self, init: B, mut f: F) -> B
    where
        Self: Sized, 
        F: FnMut(B, Self::Item) -> B,
    {
        // apply `f` to the buffered first element
        let accum = 
            if let Some(item) = self.peek.take() {
                f(init, item)
            } else {
                init
            };

        let element = &self.element;

        // apply `f` to the remaining elements
        self.iter.fold(accum,
            |mut accum, item| {
                // first, apply `f` to the separator
                accum = f(accum, element.clone());
                // then, apply `f` to the next element from the iterator
                f(accum, item)
            })
    }
```

